ions just  around the operational side of things so  just from doing that the managers were  able to build up a little bit of a  picture  about each member of staff in terms of  their family circumstances  which ones had very young children at  home  particularly i'm aware of two cases i  think where we had  issues where they felt very isolated and  in those cases  um the service managers and also the  head of service was very proactively  involved  um in making sure that that person was  supported as much as possible offering  things like  annual leave to have a bit of a rest  also offering um the ability for them to  come into the office  um and also kind of buddying up with  other people that wanted to come in the  office they were both in on the same day  within the covid uh restrictions but  allowing them  uh um to be able to see other people and  to have conversations  in the office so that was very much done  on a supervisor and head of service  level  um also one of the things that i was  really encouraged by  um and i know a lot of you won't be fans  of facebook or  kind of social media but ins to some  extent if people saw  some of their colleagues struggling on  social media they  reported that in as well so if for  instance somebody was putting a little  bit of a strange message on social media  very late at night about being lonely or  all those kinds of things they were  being picked up by colleagues and then  making sure that that person was phoned  the next day and discussing those  issues with them so it wasn't just a  workplace thing it was more of a  friendship group as well that was set up  and they also used whatsapp in some  some areas so set up working groups in  whatsapp  chat groups to be able to continually  stay in contact  um and having some informal zoom  meetings as well so not just work  based zoom meetings but kind of a coffee  morning to  for people to zoom in with workplace  issues but also  checking up that everybody was was okay  